<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT AUSTRALIA BY 109 RUNS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA BEAT AUSTRALIA BY 109 RUNS.</headline>
<dateline>BLOEMFONTEIN 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa beat Australia</p>
<p>by 109 runs in the seventh and final one day international on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>Scores: South Africa 310-6 innings closed (Lance Klusener</p>
<p>92, Hansie Cronje 69, Daryll Cullinan 57 not out), Australia 210</p>
<p>in 37 overs (Steve Waugh 91). Australia win the series 4-3.</p>
</text>
